[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648606848","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102656#issuecomment-2648606848","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102656","id":2648606848,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d3oiA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T16:33:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T16:35:10Z","body":"- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101562 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83679.\n\nI'm guessing Snap Controls to Pixels is always relative to the base viewport size, not the current window size (and current viewport resolution).\n\nHowever, I'm not sure this is what you are noticing here. Snap Controls to Pixels does **not** perform integer scaling, so if you are resizing the window, you will be getting fractional scale factors (which makes nearest-neighbor-filtered textures look bad). You need to set the stretch scale policy to `integer` in the Project Settings for that to happen instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648606848/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648874106","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102656#issuecomment-2648874106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102656","id":2648874106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d4px6","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T18:18:53Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T01:01:04Z","body":"Setting the stretch policy to integer doesn't solve the problem, it doesn't have any effect with stretch mode \"disabled\".\n\nIf you check in the MRP, the control is _not actually being resized_. It stays the same size no matter the size of the window, it just seems to pick up some kind of noise. I'm suspecting it might be a floating point precision problem in some transforms, from multiplying then dividing with the scale value.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2648874106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650243668","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102656#issuecomment-2650243668","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102656","id":2650243668,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d94JU","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T09:26:37Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T10:00:43Z","body":"Using a larger `content_scale_factor` really shows what's happening, it's not even a pixel jitter or a fp precision thing. Controls are just straight up scaled wrong based on the window size. \n\nThis is with `content_scale_factor = 8.0`:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3cf1038a-1958-488d-acf5-fd5148140f8e\n\nAgain, stretch mode is set to \"disabled\", there should be _nothing_ happening to control nodes when resizing the window.\n\nAlso, the wiggle is the exact same even with texture filtering set to linear, it's just less noticeable on small filtered textures. \n\nTurning off Snap Controls to Pixels also seems to have no effect, so I'm not sure about the relation to #83679","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2650243668/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651411519","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102656#issuecomment-2651411519","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102656","id":2651411519,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eCVQ_","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T16:45:56Z","updated_at":"2025-02-11T16:45:56Z","body":"I wonder if this is what causes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/86563.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651411519/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651848598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102656#issuecomment-2651848598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102656","id":2651848598,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eD_-W","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-11T19:19:40Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T01:08:56Z","body":"Could very well be!\n\nI found out that this is not limited to controls after all, I was just correcting everything else with a camera transform in my original project. Without that, everything in the window is rendered with the wrong scale at certain resolutions.\n\nI dug around a little bit and I think the cause is that content scale is implemented using the size override in the Viewport/Window class. But size override is clamped to integers, so only resolutions that divide by content_scale_factor result in a correct scaling.\n\nI'll try and patch it out tonight, see if it breaks anything if I allow the override value to be a float.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2651848598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2657208826","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102656#issuecomment-2657208826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102656","id":2657208826,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eYcn6","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T16:55:50Z","updated_at":"2025-02-14T11:50:22Z","body":"@Calinou  I've checked, the fix for this doesn't directly fix #86563, but the problem could have been partially caused by this.\n\nThere are some more integer values in the calculations for the different aspect ratios and stretch modes, but they are a bit more complex and harder to follow than the one for stretch mode \"disabled\" :) Maybe someone who has more experience with the aspect and viewport calculations could take a second look at it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2657208826/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]